/a><!--TRACK_AWESOME_REPO_ITEM_START____{\"type\":\"repo\",\"stargazerCount\":12,\"repo\":\"jcdavison/to_eat_app\"}____TRACK_AWESOME_REPO_ITEM_END--> - A sample graphql/rails/relay application with a related 3-part article series.</li>","updatedAt":"2021-11-20T12:27:30.000Z"},{"awesomeListRepo":"chentsulin/awesome-graphql","categoryHTML":"<h2>Databases</h2>","itemHTML":"<li><a href=\"https://www.lunasec.io/\">LunaSec</a> - Key-Value Database for encrypting/tokenizing sensitive data with <a href=\"https://www.lunasec.io/docs/pages/getting-started/dedicated-tokenizer/graphql/\">GraphQL support</a> to authorize requests. - <a href=\"https://github.com/lunasec-io/lunasec\">Source Code</a><a data-role=\"trackawesomelist-badge\" href=\"https://github.com/lunasec-io/lunasec\" style=\"text-decoration:none;top: -2px;position: relative;margin-left:4px;margin-right:4px;font-weight:400;\"><span style=\"color: #fff;font-size: 11px;font-family: Verdana, Geneva, DejaVu Sans,sans-serif;\"><span style=\"padding:4px 4px 4px 6px;background: #555;border-top-left-radius: 4px;border-bottom-left-radius: 4px;\">stars</span><span style=\"padding: 4px 6px 4px 4px;background: #007ec6;border-top-right-radius: 4px;border-bottom-right-radius: 4px;\">62</span></span></a><!--TRACK_AWESOME_REPO_ITEM_START____{\"type\":\"repo\",\"stargazerCount\":62,\"repo\":\"lunasec-io/lunasec\"}____TRACK_AWESOME_REPO_ITEM_END--></li>","updatedAt":"2021-11-20T12:27:30.000Z"},{"awesomeListRepo":"chentsulin/awesome-graphql","categoryHTML":"<h2>Implementations</h2><h4>Servers</h4>","itemHTML":"<li><a href=\"https://github.com/ryanhs/graphql-koa-scripts\">graphql-koa-scripts</a><a data-role=\"trackawesomelist-badge\" href=\"https://github.com/ryanhs/graphql-koa-scripts\" style=\"text-decoration:none;top: -2px;position: relative;margin-left:4px;margin-right:4px;font-weight:400;\"><span style=\"color: #fff;font-size: 11px;font-family: Verdana, Geneva, DejaVu Sans,sans-serif;\"><span style=\"padding:4px 4px 4px 6px;background: #555;border-top-left-radius: 4px;border-bottom-left-radius: 4px;\">stars</span><span style=\"padding: 4px 6px 4px 4px;background: #007ec6;border-top-right-radius: 4px;border-bottom-right-radius: 4px;\">0</span></span></a><!--TRACK_AWESOME_REPO_ITEM_START____{\"type\":\"repo\",\"stargazerCount\":0,\"repo\":\"ryanhs/graphql-koa-scripts\"}____TRACK_AWESOME_REPO_ITEM_END--> - GraphQL Koa 1 file simplified. usefull for quick test</li>","updatedAt":"2021-11-20T12:20:04.000Z"},{"awesomeListRepo":"chentsulin/awesome-graphql","categoryHTML":"<h2>Implementations</h2><h4>Miscellaneous</h4>","itemHTML":"<li><a href=\"https://github.com/Comcast/graphvinci\">GraphVinci</a><a data-role=\"trackawesomelist-badge\" href=\"https://github.com/Comcast/graphvinci\" style=\"text-decoration:none;top: -2px;position: relative;margin-left:4px;margin-right:4px;font-weight:400;\"><span style=\"color: #fff;font-size: 11px;font-family: Verdana, Geneva, DejaVu Sans,sans-serif;\"><span style=\"padding:4px 4px 4px 6px;background: #555;border-top-left-radius: 4px;border-bottom-left-radius: 4px;\">stars</span><span style=\"padding: 4px 6px 4px 4px;background: #007ec6;border-top-right-radius: 4px;border-bottom-right-radius: 4px;\">15</span></span></a><!--TRACK_AWESOME_REPO_ITEM_START____{\"type\":\"repo\",\"stargazerCount\":15,\"repo\":\"Comcast/graphvinci\"}____TRACK_AWESOME_REPO_ITEM_END--> - An interactive schema visualizer for GraphQL APIs.</li>","updatedAt":"2021-11-20T12:16:42.000Z"},{"awesomeListRepo":"hangtwenty/dive-into-machine-learning","categoryHTML":"<h2>Jargon note</h2>","itemHTML":"<li>Another handy term: <a href=\"https://towardsdatascience.com/who-is-a-data-engineer-how-to-become-a-data-engineer-1167ddc12811?gi=67df10cc32ea\">\"Data Engineering\"</a>, which might involve or support ML, but it's not limited to ML. <a href=\"https://ml-ops.org/\">\"MLOps\"</a> overlaps with Data Eng, and there's <a href=\"#production-deployment-mlops\">an introductory MLOps section later in this guide</a>.</li>","updatedAt":"2021-11-20T03:09:56.000Z"},{"awesomeListRepo":"hangtwenty/dive-into-machine-learning","categoryHTML":"<h2>Other courses</h2>","itemHTML":"<li><a href=\"http://stronginference.com/Bios8366/lectures.html\">Advanced Statistical Computing (Vanderbilt BIOS8366)</a>. Interactive.</li>","updatedAt":"2021-11-20T03:09:56.000Z"},{"awesomeListRepo":"hangtwenty/dive-into-machine-learning","categoryHTML":"<h2>Other courses</h2>","itemHTML":"<li>There are more alternatives linked <a href=\"#more-ways-to-dive-into-machine-learning\">at the bottom of this guide</a></li>","updatedAt":"2021-11-20T03:09:56.000Z"},{"awesomeListRepo":"hangtwenty/dive-into-machine-learning","categoryHTML":"<h2>Supplement: Learning Pandas well</h2>","itemHTML":"<li><strong>Essential</strong>: <a href=\"http://nbviewer.jupyter.org/github/rasbt/python_reference/blob/master/tutorials/things_in_pandas.ipynb\">Things in Pandas I Wish I'd Had Known Earlier</a> (as a Jupyter Notebook)</li>","updatedAt":"2021-11-20T03:09:56.000Z"},{"awesomeListRepo":"hangtwenty/dive-into-machine-learning","categoryHTML":"<h2>Deep Learning</h2><h3>Easier sharing of deep learning models and demos</h3>","itemHTML":"<li><strong><a href=\"https://replicate.ai\">replicate.ai</a> \"makes it easy to share a running machine learning model\"</strong> for the sake of reproducible research.\n<ul>\n<li>For beginners, you can try some models using GANs and other Deep Learning concepts.</li>\n<li>Join/bookmark so you can contribute a model of your own later on</li>\n<li>Open source tools: <a href=\"https://github.com/replicate/cog\"><code>cog</code></a>, <a href=\"https://github.com/replicate/keepsake\"><code>keepsake</code></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>","updatedAt":"2021-11-20T03:09:56.000Z"},{"awesomeListRepo":"hangtwenty/dive-into-machine-learning","categoryHTML":"<h2>Big data</h2>","itemHTML":"<li><a href=\"https://simplystatistics.org/2014/05/22/10-things-statistics-taught-us-about-big-data-analysis/\">10 things statistics taught us about big data analysis</a> (and some more food for thought: <a href=\"http://www.datasciencecentral.com/profiles/blogs/what-statisticians-think-about-data-scientists\">\"What Statisticians think about Data Scientists\"</a>)</li>","updatedAt":"2021-11-20T03:09:56.000Z"},{"awesomeListRepo":"hangtwenty/dive-into-machine-learning","categoryHTML":"<h2>Big data</h2>","itemHTML":"<li><a href=\"http://www.thetalkingmachines.com/blog/2015/6/4/the-economic-impact-of-machine-learning-and-using-the-kernel-trick-to-dig-in-to-big-data\">\"Talking Machines\" #12</a>: Interviews Prof. Andrew Ng (from <a href=\"https://www.coursera.org/learn/machine-learning\">our main course, which has its own module on big data</a>); this episode covers some problems relevant to <em>high-dimensional</em> data</li>","updatedAt":"2021-11-20T03:09:56.000Z"},{"awesomeListRepo":"hangtwenty/dive-into-machine-learning","categoryHTML":"<h2>Big data</h2>","itemHTML":"<li><a href=\"http://www.thetalkingmachines.com/blog/2015/7/16/really-really-big-data-and-machine-learning-in-business\">\"Talking Machines\" #15: \"Really Really Big Data and Machine Learning in Business\"</a></li>","updatedAt":"2021-11-20T03:09:56.000Z"},{"awesomeListRepo":"hangtwenty/dive-into-machine-learning","categoryHTML":"<h2>Big data</h2>","itemHTML":"<li>Free eBook, <a href=\"https://www.tamr.com/landing-pages/getting-data-right/\"><em>Getting Data Right: Tackling the Challenges of\nBig Data Volume and Variety</em></a> by Michael Stonebraker, Tom Davenport, James Markarian, and others, published by O'Reilly. You can <a href=\"http://radar.oreilly.com/2015/06/the-future-of-data-at-scale.html\">listen to an accompanying podcast</a> too.</li>","updatedAt":"2021-11-20T03:09:56.000Z"},{"awesomeListRepo":"hangtwenty/dive-into-machine-learning","categoryHTML":"<h2>More Data Science materials</h2>","itemHTML":"<li><strong><a href=\"https://jakevdp.github.io/PythonDataScienceHandbook/\">Python Data Science Handbook, as Jupyter Notebooks</a></strong></li>","updatedAt":"2021-11-20T03:09:56.000Z"},{"awesomeListRepo":"hangtwenty/dive-into-machine-learning","categoryHTML":"<h2>More Data Science materials</h2>","itemHTML":"<li>Accessible data science book, no coding experience required: <a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/book/show/17682206-data-smart\"><em>Data Smart</em> by John Foreman</a></li>","updatedAt":"2021-11-20T03:09:56.000Z"},{"awesomeListRepo":"hangtwenty/dive-into-machine-learning","categoryHTML":"<h2>More Data Science materials</h2>","itemHTML":"<li><a href=\"https://cacm.acm.org/blogs/blog-cacm/169199-data-science-workflow-overview-and-challenges/fulltext\">Data Science Workflow: Overview and Challenges</a> (read the article <em>and also</em> the comment by Joseph McCarthy)</li>","updatedAt":"2021-11-20T03:09:56.000Z"},{"awesomeListRepo":"hangtwenty/dive-into-machine-learning","categoryHTML":"<h2>More Data Science materials</h2><h3>Optional: Bayesian Statistics and Machine Learning</h3>","itemHTML":"<li>The <strong>free book</strong> <em><a href=\"http://camdavidsonpilon.github.io/Probabilistic-Programming-and-Bayesian-Methods-for-Hackers/\">Probabilistic Programming and Bayesian Methods for Hackers</a></em>. Made with a \"computation/understanding-first, mathematics-second point of view.\" It's available in print too!</li>","updatedAt":"2021-11-20T03:09:56.000Z"},{"awesomeListRepo":"hangtwenty/dive-into-machine-learning","categoryHTML":"<h2>More Data Science materials</h2><h3>Optional: Bayesian Statistics and Machine Learning</h3>","itemHTML":"<li><a href=\"https://github.com/markdregan/Bayesian-Modelling-in-Python\">Bayesian Modelling in Python</a><a data-role=\"trackawesomelist-badge\" href=\"https://github.com/markdregan/Bayesian-Modelling-in-Python\" style=\"text-decoration:none;top: -2px;position: relative;margin-left:4px;margin-right:4px;font-weight:400;\"><span style=\"color: #fff;font-size: 11px;font-family: Verdana, Geneva, DejaVu Sans,sans-serif;\"><span style=\"padding:4px 4px 4px 6px;background: #555;border-top-left-radius: 4px;border-bottom-left-radius: 4px;\">stars</span><span style=\"padding: 4px 6px 4px 4px;background: #007ec6;border-top-right-radius: 4px;border-bottom-right-radius: 4px;\">2.3k</span></span></a><!--TRACK_AWESOME_REPO_ITEM_START____{\"type\":\"repo\",\"stargazerCount\":2324,\"repo\":\"markdregan/Bayesian-Modelling-in-Python\"}____TRACK_AWESOME_REPO_ITEM_END-->. This uses <a href=\"https://github.com/pymc-devs/pymc\">PyMC</a><a data-role=\"trackawesomelist-badge\" href=\"https://github.com/pymc-devs/pymc\" style=\"text-decoration:none;top: -2px;position: relative;margin-left:4px;margin-right:4px;font-weight:400;\"><span style=\"color: #fff;font-size: 11px;font-family: Verdana, Geneva, DejaVu Sans,sans-serif;\"><span style=\"padding:4px 4px 4px 6px;background: #555;border-top-left-radius: 4px;border-bottom-left-radius: 4px;\">stars</span><span style=\"padding: 4px 6px 4px 4px;background: #007ec6;border-top-right-radius: 4px;border-bottom-right-radius: 4px;\">6.2k</span></span></a><!--TRACK_AWESOME_REPO_ITEM_START____{\"type\":\"repo\",\"stargazerCount\":6184,\"repo\":\"pymc-devs/pymc\"}____TRACK_AWESOME_REPO_ITEM_END-->, like #1.</li>","updatedAt":"2021-11-20T03:09:56.000Z"},{"awesomeListRepo":"hangtwenty/dive-into-machine-learning","categoryHTML":"<h2>More Data Science materials</h2><h3>Optional: Bayesian Statistics and Machine Learning</h3>","itemHTML":"<li>Like learning by playing? Me too. Try <a href=\"https://github.com/fulldecent/19-questions\">19 Questions</a><a data-role=\"trackawesomelist-badge\" href=\"https://github.com/fulldecent/19-questions\" style=\"text-decoration:none;top: -2px;position: relative;margin-left:4px;margin-right:4px;font-weight:400;\"><span style=\"color: #fff;font-size: 11px;font-family: Verdana, Geneva, DejaVu Sans,sans-serif;\"><span style=\"padding:4px 4px 4px 6px;background: #555;border-top-left-radius: 4px;border-bottom-left-radius: 4px;\">stars</span><span style=\"padding: 4px 6px 4px 4px;background: #007ec6;border-top-right-radius: 4px;border-bottom-right-radius: 4px;\">15</span></span></a><!--TRACK_AWESOME_REPO_ITEM_START____{\"type\":\"repo\",\"stargazerCount\":15,\"repo\":\"fulldecent/19-questions\"}____TRACK_AWESOME_REPO_ITEM_END-->, \"a machine learning game which asks you questions and guesses an object you are thinking about,\" and <strong>explains which Bayesian statistics techniques are being used.</strong></li>","updatedAt":"2021-11-20T03:09:56.000Z"},{"awesomeListRepo":"hangtwenty/dive-into-machine-learning","categoryHTML":"<h2>Risks</h2><h3>Production, Deployment, <a href=\"https://ml-ops.org/\">MLOps</a></h3>","itemHTML":"<li><a href=\"https://valohai.com/blog/the-mlops-stack/\">MLOps Stack Template</a> by Henrik Skogström</li>","updatedAt":"2021-11-20T00:24:03.000Z"},{"awesomeListRepo":"hangtwenty/dive-into-machine-learning","categoryHTML":"<h2>Risks</h2><h3>Production, Deployment, <a href=\"https://ml-ops.org/\">MLOps</a></h3>","itemHTML":"<li><a href=\"https://towardsdatascience.com/lessons-on-ml-platforms-from-netflix-doordash-spotify-and-more-f455400115c7\">Lessons on ML Platforms from Netflix, DoorDash, Spotify, and more</a> by Ernest Chan in <em>Towards Data Science</em></li>","updatedAt":"2021-11-20T00:24:03.000Z"},{"awesomeListRepo":"hangtwenty/dive-into-machine-learning","categoryHTML":"<h2>Risks</h2><h3>Production, Deployment, <a href=\"https://ml-ops.org/\">MLOps</a></h3>","itemHTML":"<li><a href=\"https://ml-ops.org/content/mlops-stack-canvas\">MLOps Stack Canvas</a> at <a href=\"https://ml-ops.org/\">ml-ops.org</a></li>","updatedAt":"2021-11-20T00:24:03.000Z"}]}},"pageContext":{"type":"day","from":1637366400000,"to":1637452799999,"previousId":"2021-11-21","nextId":"2021-11-19","nextName":"Nov 19th, 2021","previousName":"Nov 21st, 2021"}},"staticQueryHashes":["228695001","2744905544","2828988102"]}